    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="0643" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.2123/20: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-22T01:00:00-05:00">February 22, 1933—1
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:38 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. My 90, February 19, 11 a.m., last sentence, sacking of Colombian Legation.
                    Diplomatic Corps today<anchor n="8" xml:id="d614-f1"/> decided that Dean,
                    speaking for the Corps, shall state politely but firmly to the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs sacking of Colombian Legation has caused a most painful
                    impression, that result of investigation is awaited with greatest interest, and
                    that Government, in the case of any new threat, must of its own initiative take
                    prompt and abundant precautions to make impossible incident similar to that of
                    the night of February 18–19.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d614-f2"/> I concurred with my
                    colleagues and trust Department will approve. Nuncio expects to see Foreign
                    Minister 22nd or 23rd and to call further meeting about 27th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d614-f1" n="8" xml:id="d614-f1-content">
                <p>February 21.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d614-f2" n="9" xml:id="d614-f2-content">
                <p>On February 23, the Nuncio presented the views of the Diplomatic Corps to the
                    Peruvian Minister for Foreign Affairs, omitting the third point regarding future
                    precautions (701.2123/33).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
